    "modifiedAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sq_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -334
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Step Sequencer\n\nA tone matrix: 16 steps × 8 notes of a scale. Click a cell to switch it on or off, drag to paint a run of them; the playhead sweeps left to right and every lit cell in its column plays (up to four at once). R scatters a random tune, C (or the Clear bang) empties the grid. Tempo, Tone (the filter) and the Scale are on the canvas.\n\nHow it works: the grid is 128 on/off values kept by a Write* → Read* pair (\"cells\"); Edit cells rewrites it each frame (the cell under a press takes the paint value). Clock counts sixteenth notes; on each new step the lit rows of the column become notes (Scale), shared out to four MonoSynth voices, which Mix into one filter, delay and reverb. Cell looks colours the grid.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 270
      }
    },
